Package: fanogrid
Title: Grid-Size Selection for Clustered Spatial Point Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Takaaki", "Aoki", email = "takaaki-aoki@biwako.shiga-u.ac.jp",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Shinsuke", "Koyama", role = "aut"),
    person("Naoya", "Fujiwara", role = "aut"))
Description: Chooses a grid size for aggregating spatial point data whose points
    are clustered. Selectors that minimise the mean integrated squared error
    assume the points fall independently, so clustering that comes from people
    moving together is read as fine-scale structure in the underlying density and
    the selected grid is finer than the data support. The Fano factor, estimated
    from the inhomogeneous K-function, measures how much of the variance in the
    cell counts exceeds the Poisson level, and it enters the cost function as a
    correction. Grid size and Fano factor are estimated together by alternating
    updates until the grid stops changing.
